# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values from your Supabase project
# settings (Project Settings → API). Never commit the real .env file.
#
# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY and their VITE_-prefixed
# duplicates are the anon/public key + project URL. They are safe to ship
# to the browser by design (Supabase's security model protects data via
# Row Level Security, not by keeping this key secret) — but there is no
# reason to also commit them to git, so this file stays a template only.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is NOT used anywhere in Stage 1 of this app.
# It bypasses Row Level Security entirely. If a later stage needs it for a
# genuinely trusted server-only operation, set it in your deployment
# platform's secret manager — never in a file that gets committed.

SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
